      "title": "Components and JSX Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Components and JSX Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Component Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A =={blue:function component}== takes props, returns JSX",
                "Name starts with a ==capital==, or `<card />` is an HTML tag",
                "UI = f(props, state): body is ==pure==, no side effects"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. JSX Is Objects",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "JSX is sugar for `jsx()` calls returning plain ==element objects==, not DOM nodes"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "const el = <h1 className=\"t\">Hi</h1>;",
                "// compiles to",
                "const el = jsx(\"h1\", { className: \"t\", children: \"Hi\" });"
              ],
              "note": "el is a plain object, not a DOM node"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Props and Renders",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Props or state change",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Function re-called",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "New element tree",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Diff, patch DOM",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Each render is a fresh ==snapshot==",
                "Props are ==read-only==: never mutate, pass new values down"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Render only computes a description. React diffs it and touches the DOM only where it changed."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "JSX Rules and Core Workflow",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "JSX Rules and Core Workflow",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. JSX Rules",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==One root==: wrap siblings in a parent or a fragment `<>...</>`",
                "==Close every tag==: `<img />`, `<input />`",
                "`{}` embeds ==expressions== (variable, call, ternary), not `if` or `for`"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "HTML",
                "JSX"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`class`",
                  "`className`"
                ],
                [
                  "`for`",
                  "`htmlFor`"
                ],
                [
                  "`onclick`, `tabindex`",
                  "`onClick`, `tabIndex`"
                ],
                [
                  "`style=\"color:red\"`",
                  "`style={{ color: 'red' }}` (object)"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Static vs Dynamic",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Written",
                "Kind",
                "Passes"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`name=\"Ada\"`",
                  "{blue:static}",
                  "a string"
                ],
                [
                  "`size={40}`",
                  "{orange:dynamic}",
                  "a number"
                ],
                [
                  "`{user.name}`",
                  "{orange:dynamic}",
                  "any expression"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Core Workflow",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Define",
                    "sub": "function Name",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Destructure",
                    "sub": "props in signature",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "x",
                    "text": "Return JSX",
                    "sub": "one root",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Render",
                    "sub": "<Name prop={value} />",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "function Avatar({ size, name }) {",
                "  return <img width={size} alt={name} />;",
                "}",
                "",
                "// <Avatar size={40} name=\"Ada\" />"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Expressions only",
              "text": "No `if` or `for` inside `{}`: use a ==ternary== or `.map()`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Lists, Keys and Conditional Rendering",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Lists, Keys and Conditional Rendering",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Lists and Keys",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==key== goes on the **outermost** element returned inside `map`",
                "Keys are ==stable== and ==unique== among siblings",
                "Use a database id, not `Math.random()`",
                "Index key + reorder, insert or delete: state lands on the {red:wrong row}, because React matches by key"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "items.map(item => (",
                "  <Row key={item.id} {...item} />",
                "))"
              ],
              "note": "stable id as key"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Conditional Rendering",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Pattern",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`c ? <A /> : <B />`",
                  "picks one of two"
                ],
                [
                  "`c && <A />`",
                  "A only when true"
                ],
                [
                  "`return null`",
                  "renders nothing"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`{count && <Badge />}` renders ==0== when count is 0",
                "Fix: `{count > 0 && <Badge />}`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Early Return and Reset",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Early return== guards first, so the main JSX stays flat"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "if (!user) return <Login />;",
                "return <Dashboard user={user} />;"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Key resets state",
              "text": "Change a component's ==key== and React remounts it, so its state resets: `<Editor key={id} />`"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Composition, Children and Fragments",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Composition, Children and Fragments",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What children Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`children` = ==special prop== holding JSX nested between the tags",
                "==Composition beats inheritance==: generic wrapper, content passed in"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "function Card({ children }) {",
                "  return <div className=\"card\">{children}</div>;",
                "}",
                "<Card>content</Card>"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Named Slots",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Slots are {blue:plain props} that accept JSX",
                "Nested content still arrives as `children`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "<Layout header={<Nav />} sidebar={<Menu />}>",
                "  main",
                "</Layout>"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Fragments",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Syntax",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`<>...</>`",
                  "Groups siblings, ==no DOM node==, no key"
                ],
                [
                  "`<Fragment key={id}>`",
                  "Needs a ==key== in a list"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Lifting Content Up",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Pass it through children",
              "text": "Avoids ==prop drilling==. Passed-in elements are **not re-rendered** when the wrapper's state changes."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Common Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Common Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Component Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Mistake",
                "Fix",
                "Why it breaks"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Component defined inside another",
                  "Move it to module level",
                  "New type each render: {red:remount, state lost}"
                ],
                [
                  "`<card />`",
                  "`<Card />`",
                  "Lowercase is an ==HTML element=="
                ],
                [
                  "`Card(props)`",
                  "`<Card {...props} />`",
                  "Calling it directly ==breaks hooks=="
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Lists and Render Mutation",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Missing `key`, or key on the **inner** element: warning and bad diffing",
                "Key goes on the element ==map returns==",
                "`items.sort()` in render ==mutates== the array; copy first"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "// wrong: key on the inner element",
                "items.map(i => <li><b key={i.id}>{i.name}</b></li>)",
                "// right: key on the returned element",
                "items.map(i => <li key={i.id}>{i.name}</li>)",
                "// copy, then sort",
                "[...items].sort(byName).map(/* ... */)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why does an inner component lose state?** New type every render, so React remounts it",
                "**Why not call `Card(props)`?** No element, so hooks run in the parent"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Capitalised, top-level, used as `<Card />`, keyed on the returned element, and ==copy before sort=="
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
